# MCP Environment Configuration Example
# Copy this file to create your own environment configuration
# Replace all placeholder values with your actual API keys and tokens

# =============================================================================
# GITHUB MCP SERVER CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================
# GitHub Personal Access Token
# Required for: Repository access, issue management, PR operations, etc.
# How to get: GitHub Settings > Developer settings > Personal access tokens > Tokens (classic)
# Scopes needed: repo, read:org, user, project, gist
GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=github_pat_XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

# =============================================================================
# SUPABASE MCP SERVER CONFIGURATION  
# =============================================================================
# Supabase Access Token
# Required for: Database operations, project management, authentication
# How to get: Supabase Dashboard > Settings > Access Tokens > Create new token
SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=sbp_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# =============================================================================
# N8N MCP SERVER CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================
# N8N Server Configuration
# These are typically set for the n8n-mcp server environment
NODE_ENV=production
LOG_LEVEL=error
MCP_MODE=stdio
DISABLE_CONSOLE_OUTPUT=true

# Optional N8N specific configurations (if needed)
# N8N_HOST=localhost
# N8N_PORT=5678
# N8N_PROTOCOL=http
# N8N_API_KEY=your_n8n_api_key_here

# =============================================================================
# ADDITIONAL ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES (if needed)
# =============================================================================
# Add any other environment variables your MCP servers might need

# Database connections
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://username:password@localhost:5432/database_name

# API endpoints
# API_BASE_URL=https://your-api-endpoint.com

# Authentication secrets
# JWT_SECRET=your_jwt_secret_here
# ENCRYPTION_KEY=your_encryption_key_here

# =============================================================================
# USAGE INSTRUCTIONS
# =============================================================================
# 1. Copy this file to create your actual environment file:
#    cp MCP_ENV.example .env.mcp
#    
# 2. Replace all placeholder values with your actual credentials
#
# 3. Update your .mcp.json to reference environment variables:
#    Instead of hardcoded values, use: "${VARIABLE_NAME}"
#
# 4. Make sure to add your environment file to .gitignore:
#    echo ".env.mcp" >> .gitignore
#
# 5. Load environment variables before starting your MCP servers
#
# SECURITY NOTE: Never commit actual API keys or tokens to version control!
